  "id": "COMPOUND:12017 - PROTEIN:6298",
  "verbalization": "Ditiocarb zinc is implicated in the regulation of Cathepsin E through a multi-step mechanism involving the dTDP-4-dehydrorhamnose 3,5-epimerase enzyme. This enzyme is a target of multiple compounds, including (+)-Verticillol, 2-Amino-3-(3-oxo-1-propen-1-yl)-2-butenedioic acid, and P-Cresol, all of which are linked to the inhibition of Cathepsin E. The shared target of these compounds suggests a common pathway in which the dTDP-4-dehydrorhamnose 3,5-epimerase acts as a critical mediator in the interaction between Ditiocarb zinc and Cathepsin E. The presence of multiple targets for the dTDP-4-dehydrorhamnose 3,5-epimerase supports the hypothesis that this enzyme is a key node in the network of interactions that underlie the observed effects of Ditiocarb zinc on Cathepsin E. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Ditiocarb zinc to modulate Cathepsin E through the inhibition of its upstream regulators, thereby influencing downstream processes involving the enzyme.",
